It's more than "sort of" cheating. Making use of wizard-stuffed bones,
even if you didn't produce it, *is* cheating.  If you do ascend with
this, I would not announce it here.

Blessed +7 Grayswandir:
best case scenario: being expert in saber and attacking an undead
silver-hating monster
   20 to 56 total damage (average 39)
worst case secnario: expert level in sabre skill against a non-undead,
non-demon, non-silver-hating monster
  18 to 32 total damage (average 24)

+25 rubber hose
large monster:
  26 to 29 total damage (average 27.5)
small monster:
  26 to 28 total damage (average 28)

So, Grayswandir *can* do more damage but doesn't *always*.

The +25 hose, however, has a +25 enchantment *to hit*, whereas +7
grayswandir has only +8 to +13.

